 LODS (AUROC = 0.75; 95% CI, 0.73-0.76; P = .20) were not statistically different but were statistically greater than that of SIRS (AUROC = 0.64; 95% CI, 0.62-0.66; P < .001 for either LODS or SOFA vs SIRS)\", is_significant:false, auc_ci_hi:0.66, auc_ci_lo:0.62, verifier_score:1.0, model_specification:\"ROC analysis, predictive validity for in-hospital mortality, ICU encounters\", predictor_canonical:\"SIRS\", ci_lo:0.62, anchor_section:\"Performance of Existing Criteria in the ICU in the UPMC Cohort\", ci_hi:0.66, outcome:\"In-hospital mortality\", anchor_bbox:\"null\", verifier_verdict:\"ok\", timing:\"Maximum score from 48 hours before to 24 hours after onset of infection\", paper_file_name:\"Seymour_2016\", effect_value:0.64, anchor_page:5, effect_type:\"AUROC\", cohort_id:\"Seymour 2016 UPMC Validation ICU subset\", auc:0.64, outcome_type:\"mortality\", effect_size_str:\"AUROC = 0.64 (95% CI, 0.62-0.66)\", prompt_id:\"predictor_extract_v1@618f1f75\"}}, {id:\"b8d7f3b61e97eee1a7b1080b\", properties:{predictors:\"SOFA\", extractor_model:\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6\", anchor_text:\"In the ICU, the predictive validity for hospital mortality using SOFA (AUROC = 0.74; 95% CI, 0.73-0.76) and LODS (AUROC = 0.75; 95% CI, 0.73-0.76; P = .20) were not statistically different but were statistically greater than that of SIRS (AUROC = 0.64; 95% CI, 0.62-0.66; P < .001 for either LODS or SOFA vs SIRS)\", is_significant:false, auc_ci_hi:0.76, auc_ci_lo:0.73, verifier_score:1.0, model_specification:\"ROC analysis, predictive validity for in-hospital mortality, ICU encounters\", predictor_canonical:\"SOFA\", ci_lo:0.73, anchor_section:\"Performance of Existing Criteria in the ICU in the UPMC Cohort\", ci_hi:0.76, outcome:\"In-hospital mortality\", anchor_bbox:\"null\", verifier_verdict:\"ok\", timing:\"Maximum score from 48 hours before to 24 hours after onset of infection\", paper_file_name:\"Seymour_2016\", effect_value:0.74, anchor_page:5, effect_type:\"AUROC\", cohort_id:\