ctate\", outcome_type:\"mortality\", effect_size_str:\"1555 (20%)\", anchor_section:\"Table 3. Characteristics of Encounters With Suspected Infection in the Primary Cohort at 12 UPMC Hospitals From 2010 to 2012 (N = 148 907)\", prompt_id:\"predictor_extract_v1@618f1f75\", outcome:\"In-hospital mortality\", anchor_bbox:\"null\"}}, {id:\"d5d7054a74f8f7c7b15aaa9d\", properties:{predictors:\"Acinetobacter infection\", extractor_model:\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6\", anchor_text:\"After adjusting for potential confounders, having no comorbid conditions and the use of antibiotics within 1 h of sepsis onset were associated with relatively lower ICU mortality in patients with sepsis. However, advanced age; high APACHE II score; comorbid cardiovascular diseases and tumors; infection with Acinetobacter, Pseudomonas, and Staphylococcus; and the use of RRT were independent risk factors for ICU mortality in patients with sepsis.\", verifier_verdict:\"partial\", timing:\"At onset of sepsis\", is_significant:false, adjustment_kind:\"multivariate\", paper_file_name:\"Wang_2020\", anchor_page:5, effect_type:\"OR\", cohort_id:\"Wang 2020 CCCST  Sepsis subgroup\", verifier_score:0.72, model_specification:\"Multivariable stepwise logistic regression adjusted for age, sex, APACHE II score, SOFA-initial score, comorbid conditions, use of MV, RRT and vasopressors, sites of infection, isolated organisms, use of antibiotics within 1h, use of antibiotics pre-sepsis, and septic shock\", predictor_canonical:\"acinetobacter\", outcome_type:\"mortality\", effect_size_str:\"infection with Acinetobacter was independent risk factor for ICU mortality in patients with sepsis\", anchor_section:\"Factors Associated With Mortality in All Patients With Sepsis\", prompt_id:\"predictor_extract_v1@618f1f75\", outcome:\"ICU mortality\", anchor_bbox:\"null\"}}, {id:\"527f21bb3a903c676a5ff529\", properties:{predictors:\"Surgery prior to infection suspected\", extractor_model:\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6\", an