tes of infection, isolated organisms, use of antibiotics within 1h, use of antibiotics pre-sepsis, and septic shock (Table 7)\", predictor_canonical:\"no_comorbidities\", ci_lo:0.38, anchor_section:\"Factors Associated With Mortality in All Patients With Sepsis\", ci_hi:0.79, outcome:\"ICU mortality\", anchor_bbox:\"null\", p_value:0.001, verifier_verdict:\"partial\", timing:\"On ICU admission\", adjustment_kind:\"multivariate\", paper_file_name:\"Wang_2020\", effect_value:0.55, anchor_page:6, effect_type:\"OR\", cohort_id:\"Wang 2020 CCCST Sepsis subgroup\", outcome_type:\"mortality\", effect_size_str:\"OR 0.55 (95% CI 0.38-0.79), p=0.001\", prompt_id:\"predictor_extract_v1@618f1f75\"}}, {id:\"89940ad1ddd4738da0c315ca\", properties:{predictors:\"SOFA\", extractor_model:\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6\", anchor_text:\"|                    | SOFA      |               0.545 |             0.725 |       0.603 |       0.325 |       1.521 |       0.480 |\", verifier_verdict:\"ok\", timing:\"Worst score during first 24 hours of ICU admission\", is_significant:false, paper_file_name:\"Liu_2019\", anchor_page:8, effect_type:\"cutoff\", cohort_id:\"Liu 2019 MIMIC-III  Total Cohort\", outcome_window_days:30, verifier_score:0.98, model_specification:\"ROC cutoff analysis, sensitivity/specificity (Table 4)\", predictor_canonical:\"SOFA\", outcome_type:\"mortality\", effect_size_str:\"Sensitivity 0.545, Specificity 0.725, PPV 0.603, NPV 0.325, LR+ 1.521, LR- 0.480\", anchor_section:\"Table 4\", prompt_id:\"predictor_extract_v1@618f1f75\", outcome:\"30-day mortality\", anchor_bbox:\"null\"}}, {id:\"a21592563251516dbbf3f70e\", properties:{predictors:\"Administration of antibiotics within 1h of sepsis onset\", extractor_model:\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6\", anchor_text:\"Our results show that initial antibiotic administration within 1 h of the onset of sepsis decreased ICU mortality by 42% in patients with sepsis (OR 0.58, 95% CI: 0.42-0.81)\", is_significant:true, verifier_score:0.95, model_specification:\"Multivariable stepwise logistic regression adjusted for age, sex, APACHE II score, SOFA-initial score, comorbid conditions, use of MV, RRT and vasopressors, sites of infection, isolated organisms, use of antibiotics within 1h, use of antibiotics pre-sepsis, and septic shock (Table 7)\", predictor_canonical:\"antibiotics_within_1h\", ci_lo:0.42, anchor_section:\"DISCUSSION\", ci_hi:0.81, outcome:\"ICU mortality\", anchor_bbox:\"null\", p_value:0.001, verifier_verdict:\"ok\", timing:\"Within 1 hour of sepsis onset\", adjustment_kind:\"multivariate\", paper_file_name:\"Wang_2020\", effect_value:0.58, anchor_page:6, effect_type:\"OR\", cohort_id:\"Wang 2020 CCCST Sepsis subgroup\", outcome_type:\"mortality\", effect_size_str:\"OR 0.58 (95% CI 0.42-0.81), p=0.001\", prompt_id:\"predictor_extract_v1@618f1f75\"}}, {id:\"5fcb85ee7ea75055cc4ad8f0\", properties:{predictors:\"Septic shock\", extractor_model:\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6\", anchor_text:\"Patients with septic shock had a nearly 3-fold increased risk of mortality than those without shock (OR 2.92, 95% CI 2.04-4.17, Table 7)\", verifier_verdict:\"ok\", timing:\"On admission to ICU or within first 48h\", is_significant:true, adjustment_kind:\"multivariate\", paper_file_name:\"Wang_2020\", effect_value:2.92, anchor_page:5, effect_type:\"OR\", cohort_id:\"Wang 2020 CCCST Sepsis subgroup\", verifier_score:1.0, model_specification:\"Multivariable stepwise logistic regression adjusted for age, sex, APACHE II score, SOFA-initial score, comorbid conditions, use of MV, RRT and vasopressors, sites of infection, isolated organisms, use of antibiotics within 1h, use of antibiotics pre-sepsis, and septic shock (Table 7)\", predictor_canonical:\"septic_shock\", ci_lo:2.04, outcome_type:\"mortality\", effect_size_str:\"OR 2.92 (95% CI 2.04-4.17)\", anchor_section:\"Factors Associated With Mortality in All Patients With Sepsis\", prompt_id:\"predictor_extract_v1@618f1f75\", ci_hi:4.17, outcome:\"ICU mortality\", anchor_bbox:\"null\"}}, {id:\"0b157fc0f43527513ce39c06\", properties:{predictors:\"30 mL/kg initial fluid resuscitation within first 3h of onset of septic shock\", extractor_model:\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6\", anchor_text:\"Achieving the resuscitation goal of 30 ml/kg during the first 3 h (OR 0.43, 95% CI, 0.30-0.63) and administering antibiotics within 1 h (OR 0.65, 95% CI, 0.46-0.92) of the onset of septic shock decreased the odds ratio for mortality in patients with septic shock ( Table 7 ).\", verifier_verdict:\"ok\", timing:\"Within first 3 hours of septic shock onset\", is_significant:true, adjustment_kind:\"multivariate\", paper_file_name:\"Wang_2020\", anchor_page:5, effect_value:0.43, effect_type:\"OR\", cohort_id:\"Wang 2020 CCCST Sepsis subgroup\", verifier_score:1.0, model_specification:\"Multivariable stepwise logistic regression adjusted for age, APACHE II score, SOFA-initial score, comorbid cardiovascular diseases, hypertension, diabetes mellitus and chronic renal failure, use of MV, RRT and vasopressors, administration of antibiotics within 1h, and 30 mL/kg fluid resuscitation within the first 3h (Table 7, septic shock subgroup)\", predictor_canonical:\"fluid_resuscitation_30ml_kg\", ci_lo:0.3, outcome_type:\"mortality\", effect_size_str:\"OR 0.43 (95% CI 0.30-0.63)\", anchor_section:\"Factors Associated With Mortality in All Patients With Sepsis\", prompt_id:\"predictor_extract_v1@618f1f75\", ci_hi:0.63, outcome:\"ICU mortality\", anchor_bbox:\"null\"}}, {id:\"002092a2fba28e4857e3b267\", properties:{predictors:\"Administration of antibiotics within 1h of onset of septic shock\", extractor_model:\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6\", anchor_text:\"Achieving the resuscitation goal of 30 ml/kg during the first 3 h (OR 0.43, 95% CI, 0.30-0.63) and administering antibiotics within 1 h (OR 0.65, 95% CI, 0.46-0.92) of the onset of septic shock decreased the odds ratio for mortality in patients with septic shock ( Table 7 ).\", verifier_verdict:\"ok\", timing:\"Within 1 hour of septic shock onset\", is_significant:true, adjustment_kind:\"multivariate\", paper_file_name:\"Wang_2020\", effect_value:0.65, anchor_page:5, effect_type:\"OR\", cohort_id:\"Wang 2020 CCCST Sepsis subgroup\", verifier_score:1.0, model_specification:\"Multivariable stepwise logistic regression adjusted for age, APACHE II score, SOFA-initial score, comorbid cardiovascular diseases, hypertension, diabetes mellitus and chronic renal failure, use of MV, RRT and vasopressors, administration of antibiotics within 1h, and 30 mL/kg fluid resuscitation within the first 3h (Table 7, septic shock subgroup)\", predictor_canonical:\"antibiotics_within_1h\", ci_lo:0.46, outcome_type:\"mortality\", effect_size_str:\"OR 0.65 (95% CI 0.46-0.92)\", anchor_section:\"Factors Associated With Mortality in All Patients With Sepsis\", prompt_id:\"predictor_extract_v1@618f1f75\", ci_hi:0.92, outcome:\"ICU mortality\", anchor_bbox:\"null\"}}, {id:\"efb8fef15f823783108663b8\", properties:{predictors:\"Lung infection site\", p_value:0.05, extractor_model:\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6\", anchor_text:\"According to the univariate analysis, lung infection was associated with high ICU mortality, and wound/soft tissue infection was associated with low mortality.\", verifier_verdict:\"partial\", timing:\"At onset of sepsis\", is_significant:false, adjustment_kind:\"univariate\", paper_file_name:\"Wang_2020\", anchor_page:5, effect_type:\"other\", cohort_id:\"Wang 2020 CCCST Sepsis subgroup\", verifier_score:0.5, model_specification:\"Univariate analysis of association with ICU mortality in patients with positive cultures (Table 6)\", predictor_canonical:\"lung_infection\", outcome_type:\"mortality\", effect_size_str:\"Associated with high ICU mortality (p<0.05)\", anchor_section:\"Factors Associated With Mortality in All Patients With Sepsis\", prompt_id:\"predictor_extract_v1@618f1f75\", outcome:\"ICU mortality\", anchor_bbox:\"null\"}}, {id:\"a80446422958778bf5c7a112\", p