justing for potential confounders, having no comorbid conditions and the use of antibiotics within 1 h of sepsis onset were associated with relatively lower ICU mortality in patients with sepsis.\", verifier_verdict:\"partial\", timing:\"On admission to ICU\", is_significant:false, adjustment_kind:\"multivariate\", paper_file_name:\"Wang_2020\", anchor_page:5, effect_type:\"OR\", cohort_id:\"Wang 2020 CCCST Sepsis subgroup\", verifier_score:0.72, model_specification:\"Multivariable stepwise logistic regression adjusted for age, sex, APACHE II score, SOFA-initial score, comorbid conditions, use of MV, RRT and vasopressors, sites of infection, isolated organisms, use of antibiotics within 1h, use of antibiotics pre-sepsis, and septic shock (Table 7)\", predictor_canonical:\"no_comorbidities\", outcome_type:\"mortality\", effect_size_str:\"OR reported as associated with relatively lower ICU mortality in patients with sepsis\", anchor_section:\"Factors Associated With Mortality in All Patients With Sepsis\", prompt_id:\"predictor_extract_v1@618f1f75\", outcome:\"ICU mortality\", anchor_bbox:\"null\"}}, {id:\"f463811dc0b5a3ca27438c31\", properties:{predictors:\"Administration of antibiotics within 1h of sepsis onset\", extractor_model:\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6\", anchor_text:\"Our results show that initial antibiotic administration within 1 h of the onset of sepsis decreased ICU mortality by 42% in patients with sepsis (OR 0.58, 95% CI: 0.42-0.81)\", verifier_verdict:\"ok\", timing:\"Within 1 hour of sepsis onset\", is_significant:true, adjustment_kind:\"multivariate\", paper_file_name:\"Wang_2020\", effect_value:0.58, anchor_page:6, effect_type:\"OR\", cohort_id:\"Wang 2020 CCCST Sepsis subgroup\", verifier_score:1.0, model_specification:\"Multivariable stepwise logistic regression adjusted for age, sex, APACHE II score, SOFA-initial score, comorbid conditions, use of MV, RRT and vasopressors, sites of infection, isolated organisms, use of antibiotics within 1h, use of antibiotics pre-sepsis, and septic shock (Table 7)\", predictor_canonical:\"antibiotics_within_1h\", ci_lo:0.42, outcome_type:\"mortality\", effect_size_str:\"OR 0.58 (95% CI: 0.42-0.81)\", anchor_section:\"DISCUSSION\", prompt_id:\"predictor_extract_v1@618f1f75\", ci_hi:0.81, outcome:\"ICU mortality\", anchor_bbox:\"null\"}}, {id:\"e28f6bbd76b3c1410ef04c38\", properties:{predictors:\"30 mL/kg initial fluid resuscitation during first 3h of septic shock onset\", extractor_model:\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6\", anchor_text:\"Achieving the resuscitation goal of 30 ml/kg during the first 3 h (OR 0.43, 95% CI, 0.30-0.63) and administering antibiotics within 1 h (OR 0.65, 95% CI, 0.46-0.92) of the onset of septic shock decreased the odds ratio for mortality in patients with septic shock ( Table 7 ).\", verifier_verdict:\"ok\", timing:\"Within first 3 hours of septic shock onset\", is_significant:true, adjustment_kind:\"multivariate\", paper_file_name:\"Wang_2020\", anchor_page:5, effect_value:0.43, effect_type:\"OR\", cohort_id:\"Wang 2020 CCCST Sepsis subgroup\", verifier_score:1.0, model_specification:\"Multivariable stepwise logistic regression adjusted for age, APACHE II score, SOFA-initial score, comorbid cardiovascular diseases, hypertension, diabetes mellitus and chronic renal failure, use of MV, RRT and vasopressors, administration of antibiotics within 1h, and 30 mL/kg fluid resuscitation within the first 3h (Table 7, septic shock subgroup)\", predictor_canonical:\"fluid_resuscitation_30ml_kg\", ci_lo:0.3, outcome_type:\"mortality\", effect_size_str:\"OR 0.43 (95% CI 0.30-0.63)\", anchor_section:\"Factors Associated With Mortality in All Patients With Sepsis\", prompt_id:\"predictor_extract_v1@618f1f75\", ci_hi:0.63, outcome:\"ICU mortality\", anchor_bbox:\"null\"}}, {id:\"9dea87e91667832d566ebf20\", properties:{predictors:\"Administration of antibiotics within 1h of septic shock onset\", extractor_model:\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6\", anchor_text:\"Achieving the resuscitation goal of 30 ml/kg during the first 3 h (OR 0.43, 95% CI, 0.30-0.63) and administering antibiotics within 1 h (OR 0.65, 95% CI, 0.46-0.92) of the onset of septic shock decreased the odds ratio for mortality in patients with septic shock ( Table 7 ).\", verifier_verdict:\"ok\", timing:\"Within 1 hour of septic shock onset\", is_significant:true, adjustment_kind:\"multivariate\", paper_file_name:\"Wang_2020\", effect_value:0.65, anchor_page:5, effect_type:\"OR\", cohort_id:\"Wang 2020 CCCST Sepsis subgroup\", verifier_score:1.0, model_specification:\"Multivariable stepwise logistic regression adjusted for age, APACHE II score, SOFA-initial score, comorbid cardiovascular diseases, hypertension, diabetes mellitus and chronic renal failure, use of MV, RRT and vasopressors, administration of antibiotics within 1h, and 30 mL/kg fluid resuscitation within the first 3h (Table 7, septic shock subgroup)\", predictor_canonical:\"antibiotics_within_1h\", ci_lo:0.46, outcome_type:\"mortality\", effect_size_str:\"OR 0.65 (95% CI 0.46-0.92)\", anchor_section:\"Factors Associated With Mortality in All Patients With Sepsis\", prompt_id:\"predictor_extract_v1@618f1f75\", ci_hi:0.92, outcome:\"ICU mortality\", anchor_bbox:\"null\"}}, {id:\"7c7be2c4b92bc2f15f670d3e\", properties:{predictors:\"Lung infection site\", extractor_model:\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6\", anchor_text:\"According to the univariate analysis, lung infection was associated with high ICU mortality, and wound/soft tissue infection was associated with low mortality.\", verifier_verdict:\"partial\", timing:\"At onset of sepsis\", is_significant:false, adjustment_kind:\"univariate\", paper_file_name:\"Wang_2020\", anchor_page:5, effect_type:\"other\", cohort_id:\"Wang 2020 CCCST Sepsis subgroup\", verifier_score:0.75, model_specification:\"Univariate analysis (Table 6)\", predictor_canonical:\"lung_infection\", outcome_type:\"mortality\", effect_size_str:\"Associated with high ICU mortality (univariate)