ohort of unselected outpatients. Arch Pathol Lab Med. 2009;133(4):628-32. https://doi.org/10.5858/133.4.628 PMID: 19391664\n27 . Dartiguelongue JB. Systemic inflammation and sepsis. Part I: storm formation. Arch Argent Pediatr. 2020;118(6):e527-35. https://doi.org/10.5546/aap.2020.eng.e527 PMID: 33231055\nBateman RM, Sharpe MD, Singer M, Ellis CG. The effect of sepsis on the erythrocyte. Int J Mol Sci. 2017;18(9):1932. https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms18091932 PMID: 28885563\nYing-yin L. Research progress in endothelial cells injury caused by oxidative stress in atherosclerosis. Med Recap. 2015.\nOyewole AO, Birch-Machin MA. Mitochondria-targeted antioxidants. FASEB J. 2015;29(12):4766-71. https://doi.org/10.1096/fj.15-275404 PMID: 26253366\nMian P , Krabbe H, van Drie-Pierik RJHM, Silderhuis V, Beishuizen A. Elevated methaemoglobin in a critically ill patient as a result of hydrogen peroxide exposure: a case study. J Clin Pharm Ther. 2021;46(5):1473-5. https://doi.org/10.1111/jcpt.13396 PMID: 33626185\nSekhar S, Pratap V, Gaurav K, Toppo S, Kamal AK, Nair R, et al. The value of the Sequential Organ Failure Assessment (SOFA) score and serum lactate level in sepsis and its use in predicting mortality. Cureus. 2023;15(7):e42683. https://doi.org/10.7759/cureus.42683 PMID: 37649942\nKim S, Yang H, Rhee B, Song H, Kim H. Predicting survival outcomes in post-cardiac arrest syndrome: the impact of combined sequential organ failure assessment score and serum lactate measurement. Med Sci Monit. 2023;29:e942119. https://doi.org/10.12659/MSM.942119 PMID: 37705234\nRaith EP , Udy AA, Bailey M, McGloughlin S, MacIsaac C, Bellomo R, et al. Prognostic accuracy of the SOFA score, SIRS criteria, and qSOFA score for in-hospital mortality among adults with suspected infection admitted to the intensive care unit. JAMA. 2017;317(3):290-300. https://doi.org/10.1001/ jama.2016.20328 PMID: 28114553\nChang L, Chen X, Lian C. The association between the non-HDL-cholesterol to HDL-cholesterol ratio and 28-day mortality in sepsis patients: a cohort study. Sci Rep. 2022;12(1):3476. https://doi. org/10.1038/s41598-022-07459-y PMID: 35241749\n\n<!-- page: 6 -->\nTable 1.  Baseline characteristics of individuals by MCV quartiles. (N=9415).\n\n| Characteristic             | Mean Cor P uscular Volume Quartile (fl)   | Mean Cor P uscular Volume Quartile (fl)   | Mean Cor P uscular Volume Quartile (fl)   | Mean Cor P uscular Volume Quartile (fl)   | P -value   |\n|----------------------------|-------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------|------------|\n| Characteristic             | Q1                                        | Q2                                        | Q3                                        | Q4                                        |            |\n| Characteristic             | 58.0-86.0                                 | 86.1-90.9                                 | 91.0-95.4                                 | 95.5-138.9                                | 95.5-138.9 |\n| No. of participants        | 2343                                      | 2317                                      | 2384                                      | 2371                                      |            |\n| Demographics               |                                           |                                           |                                           |                                           |            |\n| Age (years)                | 62.15 ± 16.52                             | 65.20 ± 16.41                             | 67.63 ± 15.22                             | 67.99 ± 14.56                             | <0.001     |\n| Gender                     |                                           |                                           |                                           |                                           | 0.128      |\n| Male                       | 1185 (50.60%)                             | 1159 (50.02%)                             | 1147 (48.11%)                             | 1131 (47.70%)                             |            |\n| Female                     | 1157 (49.40%)                             | 1158 (49.98%)                             | 1237 (51.89%)                             | 1240 (52.30%)                             |            |\n| BMI                        | 29.68 ± 10.01                             | 29.61 ± 9.33                              | 28.51 ± 8.56                              | 28.32 ± 8.49                              | <0.001     |\n| Vital signs                |                                           |                                           |                                           |                                           |            |\n| Temperature(°C)            | 36.62 ± 1.33                              | 36.62 ± 1.33                              | 36.59 ± 1.38                              | 36.51 ± 1.19                              | 0.003      |\n| Respiratory rate (bpm)     | 31.20 ± 14.40                             | 30.26 ± 14.23                             | 30.81 ± 14.59                             | 29.94 ± 14.76                             | 0.016      |\n| Heart rate (/min)          | 115.26 ± 28.15                            | 114.72 ± 28.29                            | 114.42 ± 28.46                            | 111.69 ± 29.45                            | <0.001     |\n| MAP(mmHg)                  | 56(48-112)                                | 56 (47-115)                               | 56(47-119)                                | 53 (45-74)                                | <0.001     |\n| Severity of illness        |                                           |                                           |                                           |                                           |            